		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=296&amp;p=2055#p2055"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Hi all,<br><br>    Modifying some code, I found the DTMF alpha keys have a strange mapping.<br><br>Currently is mapped like this:<br><strong class="text-strong">A:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;LEFT&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">B:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;RIGHT&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">C:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;UP&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">D:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;DOWN&gt;</em><br><br>So, I think a more logical mapping can be defined as the following:<br>1) <strong class="text-strong">A:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;LEFT&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">B:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;UP&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">C:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;DOWN&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">D:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;RIGHT&gt;</em><br><br>or, circular one:<br>2) <strong class="text-strong">A:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;LEFT&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">B:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;UP&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">C:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;RIGHT&gt;</em> <strong class="text-strong">D:</strong><em class="text-italics">&lt;DOWN&gt;</em><br><br><br>Do you have any opinion ?<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel</div></blockquote>I would prefer new option 1). And yes it makes sense to change it from the current mapping which is not intuitive.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=102">W0RMT</a> — Mon Dec 09, 2019 3:02 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
